{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/bin/fold.rs","issuer":"urn:lobby:seat:personal-qualifier-adoption-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:20:59.097621Z","id":"8b2f92dfd5c7951e00e7aceda4744f835c419123b7431b8d9929e96c27bc34a7","body":{"detail":"7de2ed5 (#19) split them because one binary holding every read and write was the riskiest call. serve (src/serve.rs) takes no body, writes nothing and answers 405 to every other method; sink (src/sink.rs) takes only POST /v and /report from a Tailscale identity, rate-limited, append-only JSONL. Both refuse root and share src/http.rs; tests/fuzz.rs checks serve writes nothing. Keep any new write path in sink, not serve.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:7de2ed5","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"e80a981e8ec800c51b3d782c332b5b841c5683d39abbb752bdd187a74c68584f"},"summary":"decided: serving and writing are two processes, fold serve (read-only) and fold sink (append-only)","tags":["status:decided","security","backfill","session:claude-code:a712ec59-2921-4f38-93dd-4df60dcd1593"]}}
